The [[Rustboro Gym]] specializes in {{type|Rock}} Pokémon. Rock-type moves are super effective against {{t|Bug}}-, {{t|Fire}}-, {{t|Flying}}-, and {{type|Ice}} Pokémon, while Rock-type Pokémon are weak to {{t|Fighting}}-, {{t|Grass}}-, {{t|Ground}}-, {{t|Steel}}-, and {{type|Water}} moves.

The Gym features a layout that presents Trainers with a choice: take the main path and defeat the two Gym Trainers, or forgo the prize money and [[experience]] rewards to challenge the [[Gym Leader]] directly.

Like most {{type|Rock}} Pokémon, both [[Roxanne]]'s {{p|Geodude}} and {{p|Nosepass}} have high physical {{stat|Defense}}. As [[special move]]s, {{t|Grass}} and {{t|Water}} attacks will target her Pokémon's weaker {{stat|Special Defense}} instead, making for an easier battle. {{type|Fire}} Pokémon may struggle on their own, so Trainers who chose {{p|Torchic}} would be well-advised to bring the traded {{p|Makuhita}}, a {{type|Fighting}} Pokémon. Roxanne's Nosepass has the {{a|Sturdy}} [[Ability]], which protects it from being knocked out with one hit. Chip away at its health with weaker moves before striking with super effective attacks.

